    "raw": "'Delight. It is nice to see you.' I said, but the Glitch just looked at me strangely, and then said something to his friend. I noticed something here, too. When the Glitch address each other, they do not use these prefix words. Perhaps something in their programming means they can read each others' tones without explanation.",
    "value": "“欣悦。很高兴见到您。”我说道。然而那电子人只是古怪地看了我一眼，随即对他的同伴说了些什么。于此，我另有发现：当电子人彼此交谈时，他们并不使用这些前缀词。或许，是他们程序中的某种设定，使其无需解释便能解读对方的语气。"
